\subsection{Prespecified Subgroups}
Subgroup analyses were prespecified for age and sex,
because treatment benefit is biologically plausible to vary
with comorbidity burden and tolerance.
The adjusted subgroup estimates are reported in Table~\ref{tab:subgroups}.

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\begin{tabular}{lcc}
\toprule
Subgroup & Adjusted HR (95\% CI) & $p$-value \\
\midrule
Age $<$ 65 years & 0.62 (0.41--0.94) & 0.025 \\
Age $\geq$ 65 years & 0.88 (0.61--1.27) & 0.492 \\
Male & 0.71 (0.48--1.05) & 0.083 \\
Female & 0.79 (0.52--1.20) & 0.268 \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\caption{Adjusted hazard ratios for recurrence in prespecified subgroups.}
\label{tab:subgroups}
\end{table}
